# Keyboard window management: Alt+Tab (release picks), Shift+Alt+Tab, Alt+F4, and Tab and Shift+Tab between the fields of a window.
desk-scenario 1
screen 640 480
depths 8 4
open notes 60 60 300 180 "Notes"
label notes 12 12 "The first window."
open welcome 220 150 340 200 "Welcome to Desk"
label welcome 12 12 "Type something:"
field welcome 12 36 300
pointer 320 240
frame open
# Alt+Tab: nothing is drawn while Alt is held, and releasing it focuses Notes, the next window down, and raises it.
key LeftAlt down
key Tab down
key Tab up
key LeftAlt up
frame notes
# Alt+Tab again goes back to Welcome, whose field has kept its caret.
key LeftAlt down
key Tab down
key Tab up
key LeftAlt up
frame welcome
# A third window, with a field of its own, opens on top; Shift+Alt+Tab goes the other way round, to the bottom window (Notes).
open memo 380 40 220 120 "Memo"
label memo 12 12 "A third window."
field memo 12 36 150
frame memo
key LeftShift down
key LeftAlt down
key Tab down
key Tab up
key LeftAlt up
key LeftShift up
frame shifted
# Two steps of one cycle: Alt+Tab twice lands two windows down, on Welcome (the stacking order is Welcome, Memo, Notes).
key LeftAlt down
key Tab down
key Tab up
key Tab down
key Tab up
key LeftAlt up
frame twosteps
# Alt+F4 closes the focused window (Welcome) and the one below it (Memo) is focused.
key LeftAlt down
key F4 down
key F4 up
key LeftAlt up
frame closed
# A window with two fields. The field added last has the focus, so the first word goes to City; Shift+Tab moves the caret to Name
# (the label between them is skipped) and the next word goes there; Tab wraps back to City, which takes one more letter.
open form 40 280 300 160 "Form"
label form 12 12 "Name"
field form 12 30 200
label form 12 64 "City"
field form 12 82 200
type "paris"
frame city
key LeftShift down
key Tab down
key Tab up
key LeftShift up
type "ada"
frame name
key Tab down
key Tab up
type "!"
frame wrapped
